description:
**Glassworks London** is an independent women’s fashion retailer founded in 2010, operating across UK retail stores, ecommerce and international production.

**THE ROLE**

We are looking for an exceptionally talented Fashion Creative Director to define and elevate the visual world of Glassworks, with an immediate focus on creating outstanding fashion photography, fashion film and campaign content.

You will bring distinctive fashion taste, strong visual storytelling and proven experience directing fashion shoots and moving-image production. Your work will shape how Glassworks looks and feels across campaigns, ecommerce homepages, advertising, social content and other customer-facing channels.

Working closely with the Founder / CEO, Marketing team and specialist producers, you will develop compelling creative concepts, select and direct talent, establish photographic and film standards, and ensure the resulting work feels recognisably Glassworks.

Beyond imagery, we would love someone capable of helping evolve the broader brand aesthetic across typography, colour, packaging, branded products, retail environments and customer experience. However, excellence in fashion photography and film direction is the essential foundation of this role.

We welcome exceptional senior Fashion Art Directors with the capability and ambition to take on broader creative leadership.

**WORKING PATTERN / LOCATION**

Flexible location and engagement structure, with remote work possible for creative development and direction. The successful candidate must be available for agreed fashion productions and other essential in-person creative work in London or relevant production locations.

Substantial part-time or retained freelance arrangements may be considered according to capability, availability and the scope of responsibility.

**KEY RESPONSIBILITIES**

* Fashion photography: Conceive and direct distinctive fashion photography for campaigns, ecommerce model imagery, ecommerce homepages, advertising, launches and other brand communications, establishing clear standards for casting, styling, lighting, composition, mood, image selection, retouching and final creative approval.
* Fashion film and videography: Develop and direct fashion films, campaign videos, motion-led content and other brand moving-image work, including creative concepts, shot direction, movement, pacing, editing approach, colour treatment, music and final creative approval.
* Creative concepts and campaign direction: Translate product, customer and marketing objectives into compelling visual concepts and narratives that build fashion desirability and support commercial performance.
* Fashion taste and brand identity: Develop and protect a distinctive Glassworks aesthetic, building on its London roots, Korean fashion influences, cultural energy, style, personality and existing creative references.
* Casting and styling: Direct the selection of models, stylists, hair and makeup talent, wardrobe, accessories and other elements contributing to the final fashion image or film.
* Creative production leadership: Work with the Creative Producer to select photographers, videographers, stylists and other specialist talent, prepare production briefs, review plans and direct the creative outcome.
* Social visual direction: Establish the creative principles for social imagery and video, including fashion aesthetics, visual storytelling, editing style and music direction, while working with Social Content & Community on platform formats, scripts, programming and audience requirements.
* AI imagery and creative technology: Guide the visual and fashion standards for AI-assisted ecommerce and campaign imagery, working with AI image creators and retouchers to maintain product accuracy, brand consistency, model quality, styling and photographic credibility.
* Brand identity development: Help refine the Glassworks visual identity, including typography, colour palette, graphic language and branded communications, recruiting and directing specialist graphic designers where appropriate.
* Packaging and branded products: Develop creative direction for packaging, tote bags, labels, swing tags, branded accessories and considered brand applications on selected products, in collaboration with Product and Buying.
* Retail and customer experience: Establish relevant creative standards for store atmosphere, music, visual communication, uniforms, packaging presentation and other physical expressions of the brand.
* Creative standards and capability: Build clear, practical visual references and creative rules, develop a strong specialist talent network, review output and enable internal teams to produce consistently on-brand work without continual Founder intervention.
* AI-forward creative practice: Actively explore AI and emerging creative technologies to improve research, concept development, visual experimentation and production efficiency while maintaining original creative judgement, technical accuracy and strong brand standards.

**WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR**

We are looking for evidence of:

* substantial professional experience in fashion creative direction or fashion art direction, with a strong portfolio of personally directed fashion photography and fashion film;
* exceptional taste in fashion styling, models, casting, image composition, lighting, photography and moving-image storytelling;
* demonstrated ability to conceive and direct commercially effective fashion campaigns from concept through final imagery;
* strong understanding of contemporary fashion, youth culture, visual trends and relevant London and Korean fashion influences;
* proven experience briefing and directing photographers, videographers, stylists, hair and makeup teams, editors and specialist creative talent;
* the ability to develop visual concepts that translate across ecommerce, advertising, campaign and social channels;
* sound judgement about budgets and production resources, with the ability to create exceptional work without relying on unnecessarily expensive production;
* a strong creative point of view combined with respect for established brand identity and the ability to recognise what should be preserved;
* confident collaboration with Marketing, Product, Retail and production teams;
* an enthusiastic, discerning approach to AI and emerging creative technology, with appropriate human review and quality control.

Experience shaping typography, colour, packaging, graphic identity, retail atmosphere or broader brand-world development would be particularly valuable.

**WHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE**

Strong performance will be visible when:

* Glassworks consistently produces distinctive, desirable fashion photography and film;
* campaigns, ecommerce model imagery, homepage imagery and advertising have a stronger and more recognisable fashion aesthetic;
* casting, styling, lighting, movement, editing, retouching and image selection meet clear creative standards;
* physical photography and AI-assisted ecommerce imagery belong to a coherent visual world;
* production teams can execute compelling fashion content from well-developed briefs;
* Social receives strong visual principles and assets while retaining the speed required for effective channel programming;
* AI-generated imagery reflects the approved brand aesthetic while accurately representing the merchandise;
* the brand's broader visual language becomes sharper, more cohesive and commercially useful;
* packaging, graphic identity and retail creative standards develop where appropriate;
* and the Founder is no longer required to personally establish, art-direct and protect every creative decision.
